==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|nummer}} {{qualifier|dialectal}}
* {{l|en|numbre}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*nem-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|number}}, {{m|enm|nombre}}, {{m|enm|numbre}}, {{m|enm|noumbre}}, from {{der|en|xno|noumbre|sc=Latn}}, {{der|en|fro|nombre|sc=Latn}}, from {{der|en|la|numerus||number}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*nem-||to divide}}. Compare {{cog|stq|Nummer}}, {{m|stq|Nuumer}}, {{cog|fy|nûmer}}, {{cog|nl|nummer||number}}, {{cog|de|Nummer||number}}, {{cog|da|nummer||number}}, {{cog|sv|nummer||number}}, {{cog|is|númer||number}}. Replaced Middle English {{m|enm|ȝetæl}} and {{m|enm|rime}}, more at {{m|en|tell}}, {{m|en|tale}} and {{m|en|rhyme}}.

