====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[abstract]] [[entity]] used to [[describe]] [[quantity]].
#: {{ux|en|Zero, one, −1, 2.5, and pi are all '''numbers'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[numeral]]: a [[symbol]] for a [[non-negative]] [[integer]].
#: {{syn|en|scalar|rime|q2=obsolete}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''number''' 8 is usually made with a single stroke.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|mathematics}} An [[element]] of one of several [[sets]]: [[natural number]]s, [[integer]]s, [[rational number]]s, [[real number]]s, [[complex number]]s, and sometimes extensions such as [[hypercomplex numbers]], etc.
#: {{ux|en|The equation <math>e^{i\pi}+1=0</math> includes the most important '''numbers''': 1, 0, <math>\pi</math>, <math>i</math>, and <math>e</math>.}}
# {{lb|en|Followed by a [[numeral]]; used [[attributive]]ly}} Indicating the position of something in a list or sequence. Abbreviations: ''[[No]]'' or ''[[No.]]'', ''[[no]]'' or ''[[no.]]'' (in each case, sometimes written with a superscript "o", like Nº or &#x2116;). The symbol "#" is also used in this manner.
#: {{ux|en|Horse '''number''' 5 won the race.}}
# [[quantity|Quantity]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-08|volume=407|issue=8839|page=52|magazine=w:The Economist|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/international/21579039-chinas-growing-empire-ports-abroad-mainly-about-trade-not-aggression-new-masters The new masters and commanders]|passage=From the ground, Colombo’s port does not look like much.{{...}}&nbsp; But viewed from high up in one of the growing '''number''' of skyscrapers in Sri Lanka’s capital, it is clear that something extraordinary is happening: China is creating a shipping hub just 200 miles from India’s southern tip.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Essayes|chapter=Of the True Greatness of Kingdoms and Estates|passage='''Number''' itself importeth not much in armies where the people are of weak courage.}}
#: {{ux|en|Any '''number''' of people can be reading from a given repository at a time.}}
# A [[sequence]] of [[digit]]s and [[letter]]s used to register people, automobiles, and various other items.
#: {{ux|en|Her passport '''number''' is C01X864TN.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|informal}} A [[telephone number]].
#* {{quote-song|en|title=w:Rikki Don't Lose That Number|artist=w:Steely Dan|year=1974|passage=Rikki, don't lose that '''number''' /  You don't wanna call nobody else  / Send it off in a letter to yourself}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=E. Forrest Hein|title=The Ruach Project,|publisher=Xulon Press|page=86
|passage=“[...] I wonder if you could get hold of him and have him call me here at Interior. I’m in my office, do you have my '''number'''?”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Lindsey Nicole Isham|title=No Sex in the City: One Virgin's Confessions on Love, Lust, Dating, and Waiting|publisher=Kregel Publications|page=111
|passage=When I agreed to go surfing with him he said, “Great, can I have your '''number'''?” Well, I don’t give my '''number''' to guys I don’t know.}}
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20170918070146/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-3-i-am-here/3126527.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: Marsha's work '''number''' is 555-8986.
#*:: {{audio|en|Marsha's work number is 555-8986.ogg|Audio (US)}}
# {{senseid|en|grammar}}{{lb|en|grammar}} Of a word or phrase, the state of being [[singular]], [[dual]] or [[plural]], shown by [[inflection]].
#: {{ux|en|Adjectives and nouns should agree in gender, '''number''', and case.}}
# {{lb|en|now|rare|in the plural}} Poetic metres; [[verse]]s, [[rhyme]]s.
#* {{RQ:Donne Poems|poem=The Triple Foole|page=204|passage=Griefe brought to '''numbers''' cannot be ſo fierce, / For, he tames it, that fetters it in verſe.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Arbuthnot|page=7|lines=124–125|passage=As yet a Child, nor yet a Fool to Fame, / I liſp'd in '''Numbers''', for the '''Numbers''' came.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[performance]]; especially, a single [[song]] or song and dance routine within a larger show.
#: {{ux|en|For his second '''number''', he sang "The Moon Shines Bright".}}
# {{lb|en|countable|informal}} A [[person]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968|author=Janet Burroway|title=The dancer from the dance: a novel,|publisher=Little, Brown|page=40
|passage=I laughed. "Don't doubt that. She's a saucy little '''number'''."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|author=w:Erica Jong|title=Serenissima,|publisher=Dell|page=214
|passage="Signorina Jessica," says the maid, a saucy little '''number''', "your father has gone to his prayers and demands that you come to the synagogue at once [...]"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Denise A. Agnew; Kate Hill; Arianna Hart|title=By Honor Bound,|publisher=Ellora's Cave Publishing|page=207
|passage=He had to focus on the mission, staying alive and getting out, not on the sexy '''number''' rubbing up against him.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|informal}} An item of [[clothing]], particularly a [[stylish]] one.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Cesca Martin|title=Agony Angel: So You Think You've Got Problems...,|publisher=Troubador Publishing Ltd|page=134
|passage=The trouble was I was wearing my backless glittering '''number''' from the night before underneath, so unless I could persuade the office it was National Fancy Dress Day I was doomed to sweat profusely in bottle blue.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Lorelei James|title=Running with the Devil|publisher=Samhain Publishing, Ltd|page=46
|passage="I doubt the sexy '''number''' you wore earlier tonight fell from the sky."}}
# {{lb|en|slang|chiefly|US}} A [[marijuana]] cigarette, or [[joint]]; also, a quantity of marijuana bought from a [[dealer]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=K'wan|title=Hoodlum|publisher=St. Martin's Press|isbn=0312333080|pageurl=https://books.google.es/books?id=qQfTHfHYgM8C&lpg=PA185&dq=%22numbers%22&hl=es&pg=PA1#v=onepage&q&f=false|page=1
|passage=These were the two that Tommy had chosen to collect a debt owed  to his family by a dude named Heath who ran '''numbers''' out of a grocery store on 131st and Lenox.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=w:Thomas Pynchon|title=Inherent Vice|page=12|publisher=Vintage|year_published=2010
|passage=Back at his place again, Doc rolled a '''number''', put on a late movie, found an old T-shirt, and sat tearing it up into short strips {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} An [[issue]] of a [[periodical]] [[publication]].
#: ''the latest '''number''' of a magazine''
# A large amount, in contrast to a smaller amount; numerical preponderance.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=May 10 1980|author=Al King|title=Braves travel to New England with reputation|journal=The Indiana Gazette
|passage=Despite last week's woes, the Braves still sport '''numbers''' that would make Christie Brinkley blush.}}

